{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-001","severity":"P2","findingType":"drift","release":"v4.0.0.8","label":"The v4.0.0.8 claim that First Use names all seven runtimes and how each spells /speckit:complete drifts from the docs: README has no First Use heading (its section is First Task) and names only Codex, Cursor, Pi and Devin at README.md:208, repeated at INSTALL-SKILLED.md:65, leaving Claude, OpenCode and dsh unnamed.","iteration":1,"sources":["README.md","INSTALL-SKILLED.md",".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.8.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-002","severity":"P2","findingType":"drift","release":"v4.0.0.3","label":"The v4.0.0.3 claim that /doctor:speckit checks spec-kit search only drifts from the route: _routes.yaml:76 adds the citation-drift census (cite-drift-scan.mjs) as a fourth invocation and speckit.md:75 offers it, which is a sk-doc documentation check rather than a search check.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml",".skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md",".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-003","severity":"P2","findingType":"drift","release":"v4.0.1.0","label":"The v4.0.1.0 claim that /doctor:symlink unlink undoes one run exactly is stronger than the documented behavior: symlink.md:92 skips a recorded path whose state no longer matches the record as 'changed since apply', so unlink is a safe best-effort reversal rather than an exact one.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md",".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.1.0.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-004","severity":"P2","findingType":"ux","release":"v4.0.0.3","label":"A healthy route-validate.sh run exits 0 but always prints 11 informational WARN: H1 duplicate-flag lines, so the one authoritative validator output never looks clean and operators are trained to skim it.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh",".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-005","severity":"P2","findingType":"extension","release":"v4.0.0.3","label":"route-validate.py D1 checks YAML assets only for the routes section (check_yaml_assets at line 414), leaving the seven standalone YAML references for /doctor:update and /doctor:env and the mcp_subroutes assets unchecked; all exist today, but deleting one would keep CI green until the command runs.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.py",".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-006","severity":"P2","findingType":"extension","release":"v4.0.1.0","label":"The linkable runtime list is duplicated in install.md:37, symlink.md:57 and symlink-manifest.json:5 with no validator cross-check; six runtimes is correct because .dsh reads no project folder by itself (.dsh/SYNC.md:8), but adding a linkable runtime needs three synchronized edits.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/install.md",".skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md",".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json",".dsh/SYNC.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter001-007","severity":"P2","findingType":"ux","release":"v4.0.0.8","label":"symlink-engine.cjs --help prints 'ERROR: unknown flag: --help' and exits 2 with no usage text or pointer to its check/plan/apply/unlink modes, so the refusal path is the only feedback an operator gets.","iteration":1,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs",".skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md"]}
